<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed SAT Instance Features</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The 21 features used to construct the feature vector for each SAT instance are detailed below, organized by category.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Basic Features:</span> These capture the overall size and scale of the instance.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_variables</span>: The number of variables (<math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V|</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_clauses</span>: The number of clauses (<math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C|</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">var_clause_ratio</span>: The ratio of variables to clauses (<math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V|/|C|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V|/|C|</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clause Structure Features:</span> These describe the properties of the clauses in the formula.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">avg_clause_length</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">std_clause_length</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">min_clause_length</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_clause_length</span>: Statistical measures of the number of literals per clause.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">clause_length_entropy</span>: The entropy of the clause length distribution, measuring its diversity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">unit_clause_ratio</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">binary_clause_ratio</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">long_clause_ratio</span>: The proportion of clauses that are unit (length 1), binary (length 2), or long (length <math id="A1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math> 5).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variable Activity Features:</span> These describe how variables are distributed across clauses.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">avg_var_frequency</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">std_var_frequency</span>, <span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_var_frequency</span>: Statistical measures of how many times each variable appears in the formula.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">var_frequency_entropy</span>: The entropy of the variable frequency distribution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">singleton_var_ratio</span>: The ratio of variables that appear in only one clause.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Polarity Features:</span> These capture the balance between positive and negative literals.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">positive_literal_ratio</span>: The overall ratio of positive literals to total literals.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">balanced_var_ratio</span>: The proportion of variables that appear an equal number of times positively and negatively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pure_literal_ratio</span>: The proportion of variables that appear with only one polarity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">polarity_bias</span>: A measure of the overall tendency towards positive or negative literals.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complexity Features:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i5.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">constraint_density</span>: A measure of how constrained the problem is, defined as the total number of literals divided by the product of variables and clauses.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
